<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korean 3-yr yields edge up in weak sentiment.</title>
<headline>S.Korean 3-yr yields edge up in weak sentiment.</headline>
<text>
<p>Yields on three-year corporates closed slightly higher on Monday in thin trading on expectations of heavy new issues later this week, brokers said.</p>
<p>Three-month CD yields and overnight call rates ended lower on improved liquidity in the short-term money market, they said.</p>
<p>* 3-yr corporates end at 12.30 pct from Saturday's 12.28</p>
<p>* 3-mth CDs close at 13.38 pct from 13.45</p>
<p>* Overnight call average 13.30 pct from 13.50</p>
</text>
